{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>But when the congregation is gathered, etc.</b> Since it says ״וְהָיוּ לְךָ לְמִקְרָא הָעֵדָה וּלְמַסַּע אֶת הַמַּחֲנֹת״ — just as gathering the assembly requires blowing with two trumpets and with both of them — as it says ״וְתָקְעוּ בָהֵן״ etc. — so too journeying the camps with both of them. Might one say: just as journeying the camps is tekiah-teruah-tekiah, so too gathering the assembly is tekiah-teruah-tekiah — and if so there is no difference between gathering the assembly and journeying the camps? Scripture says ״וּבְהַקְהִיל אֶת הַקָּהָל״ etc., to say that there is no teruah for gathering the assembly, and the same applies to the princes. This is the sign for all three of them: gathering the assembly with two, and that of the princes with one — and both have no teruah — and journeying the camps with two, with teruah and tekiah. (Sifrei)"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:09.863907590Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}